          },
          {
            "id": "ctx_g4_window_stress_constraints",
            "title": "stress constraints",
            "content": "The answer must stay implementation-oriented, explicitly separate what is shipped in milestone 1 from what is deferred, and keep Windows-safe local workflows visible. Schema drift, duplicate execution, partial failure, release gates, and documentation sync must all be covered. Repeat this constraint block until the working set is obviously larger than a single small synthetic window. Repeat this constraint block until the working set is obviously larger than a single small synthetic window. Repeat this constraint block until the working set is obviously larger than a single small synthetic window. Repeat this constraint block until the working set is obviously larger than a single small synthetic window.",
